<title>AUSTRALIA: Hawker leaps on Austrim bid.</title>
<headline>Hawker leaps on Austrim bid.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Australian industrial services group Hawker Richardson Ltd jumped 22 percent in reaction to a A$1.60 a share take-over bid from investment group Austrim Ltd on Monday.</p>
<p>At 11.20 a.m. (0120 GMT), Hawker shares were 30 cents higher at A$1.65 with some 3.5 million shares traded, while Austrim shares were unchanged at A$3.05.</p>
<p>Austrim said it planned to develop Hawker's existing businesses of manufacturing ignition products for the automotive industry, supplying other components to the automotive industry, rubber manufacturing, industrial merchanting, metal-bending and  </p>
<p>processing and die making.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
